# ==============================================================================
# INCEPTION ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES EXAMPLE
# ==============================================================================
# 
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file and rename it to `.env` (e.g. `cp .env_example .env`).
# 2. Update DOMAIN_NAME with your actual 42 login.
# 3. Ensure that your actual `.env` file is never committed to Git!
# 
# IMPORTANT: DOCKER SECRETS VS .ENV
# By default, this project uses Docker secrets for security. You must create 
# files in the `secrets/` directory (e.g., `secrets/mysql_database.txt`) containing 
# the actual values for the credentials below. 
#
# If you prefer to rely solely on this `.env` file instead of Docker secrets, you 
# can uncomment the variables below and comment out the variable redefinitions 
# at the start of the `docker-entrypoint.sh` files.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOMAIN CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The domain name used by NGINX to route external traffic to WordPress.
# According to the subject, this MUST be your intra login followed by '.42.fr'
# (e.g., spacotto.42.fr).
DOMAIN_NAME=login.42.fr

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MARIADB (DATABASE) CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The name of the database that WordPress will use to store all its data.
# MYSQL_DATABASE=wordpress

# The standard database user that WordPress will use to connect.
# NOTE: The subject requires that this username cannot contain "admin" or 
# "administrator".
# MYSQL_USER=your_db_user

# The password for the standard database user. 
# MYSQL_PASSWORD=your_db_password

# The root password for the MariaDB instance. 
# MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=your_db_root_password

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORDPRESS CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The administrator account details. 
# REMINDER: Subject strictly forbids the username containing "admin" or "administrator".
# WP_ADMIN_USER=your_super_user
# WP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=your_super_password
# WP_ADMIN_EMAIL=your_super_email@example.com

# The secondary user account details required by the subject.
# WP_USER=your_normal_user
# WP_USER_PASSWORD=your_normal_password
# WP_USER_EMAIL=your_normal_email@example.com
